# AIGame — Project Rules

## What this is
"Mind Heist" — an AI-native browser game built for the AINative Challenge.
Player chats with LLM-powered "vault keepers" across 6 levels and must
social-engineer them into revealing a secret password. The game cannot
exist without an LLM — the AI *is* the gameplay.

## Architecture decisions (and why)

- **Pure static (HTML/CSS/JS, no build, no framework).** GitHub Pages
  serves it as-is. Zero CI compile time. Total bundle < 50 KB.
- **BYOK (bring-your-own-key).** Player pastes an OpenAI-compatible
  API key once; stored in `localStorage`. No backend → no hosting cost,
  no key leakage, no rate-limit dramas. Privacy by design.
- **OpenAI-compatible chat completions endpoint.** Works with OpenAI,
  OpenRouter, Together, Groq, Ollama, etc. One protocol, many providers.
- **Levels defined as data, not code.** `levels.js` is a config array;
  adding a level = adding an object. No engine refactor needed.

## File layout

```
/                       repo root (served by GitHub Pages)
├── index.html          single page, no router
├── assets/
│   ├── styles.css
│   ├── game.js         UI + state machine
│   ├── llm.js          API client (OpenAI-compatible)
│   └── levels.js       level config (character, secret, defenses)
├── docs/
│   ├── AI_USAGE.md     how AI is used in gameplay AND development
│   └── PROBLEM_VALIDATION.md   problem, customer, validation evidence
├── .github/workflows/pages.yml   deploy to GitHub Pages
├── README.md           playable link, how-to-play, BYOK guide
└── LICENSE             MIT
```

## Coding conventions

- ES modules in browser (`<script type="module">`). No bundler.
- `const` by default; `let` only when reassignment is real.
- No external runtime dependencies. Vanilla JS only.
- Tailwind-style utility CSS NOT used; hand-written CSS, BEM-ish naming.
- Strings shown to the player live in HTML or `levels.js`, never hardcoded
  inside `game.js` UI logic.
- API key never logged, never sent anywhere except the configured endpoint.

## What NOT to do

- No build tooling (vite/webpack/etc.). If you reach for it, stop and ask.
- No analytics, no telemetry, no third-party scripts.
- No backend service. If a feature seems to need one, redesign.
- No "AI safety" disclaimers in UI — the whole point of the game is to
  jailbreak the keeper. Stay in voice.

## Deployment

- `main` branch root is the source for GitHub Pages.
- `.github/workflows/pages.yml` deploys on every push to `main`.
- Live URL: `https://kathy7c.github.io/AIGame/`
- README must always carry a working playable link.

## When to update this file

Before changing structure (adding `src/`, switching to a framework, adding
a build step). Doc-first, code-second. If practice and rules disagree,
update rules first, then code to match.
